<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia to ship 120,000/tn wheat to Sudan - AWB.</title>
<headline>Australia to ship 120,000/tn wheat to Sudan - AWB.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia will supply 120,000 tonnes of hard wheat to the Sagya flour mill in Khartoum, Sudan over the next 12 months, the Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said on Friday.</p>
<p>The first of six 20,000-tonne shipments will be loaded in Australia at the end of July, the AWB aid.</p>
<p>The supply contract was reached last week in London, the AWB said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
